{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788132865,"nonce":"a8gAdJiVV2n70Gx/LZkneRjxo6k=","message":"AMENDMENT from the learning-helper/curriculum audit — orchestrator, session 4.\nTwo observation blind spots that only this spec can close, because vanilla gives\nno alert for either.\n\n**1. No `forbidden` field is planned, and every drop-pod colony start needs one.**\nThe scope's things rollups (def/count/quality/HP) have no forbidden flag. This\nis not a tutorial curiosity: `ScenPart_PlayerPawnsArriveMethod.DoDropPods` calls\n`DropThingGroupsNear(..., forbid: true, ...)`, so **a drop-pod start lands with\nits own gear forbidden** — which is why the scripted tutorial's second action is\n`UnforbidStartingResources`. Without a forbidden flag or count, \"why is nothing\nbeing hauled\" has no diagnostic path at all.\n\n**2. Fires outside the home area are invisible, not merely late.**\n`Alert_FireInHomeArea` is scoped to `areaManager.Home[thing.Position]`, and no\nother vanilla alert covers fire. The game hedges this itself: `Verse/Fire.cs:118`\nteaches the `HomeArea` concept on EVERY fire spawn regardless of location. Our\nalert section is a verbatim passthrough of the readout, so a fire on unclaimed\nground is a total blind spot. **A map-level \"any Fire, home area or not\" scan\nbelongs here and must not depend on the alert readout.**\n\n**3. No shelter/deterioration signal.** The `Deterioration` concept names real\nsilent attrition — items left outdoors decay — and there is no vanilla alert for\nit (all 132 checked). A roofed/sheltered field on thing rollups is the only\nplace a leading signal can originate.\n\n**4. Animal state is observed even though animal management is deferred.** See\nDESIGN's new non-goals entry: seven vanilla alerts hang off animals\n(`AnimalPenNeeded`, `AnimalPenNotEnclosed`, `PennedAnimalHungry`, `PredatorInPen`,\n`AnimalRoaming`, `StarvationAnimals`, `HypothermicAnimals`). The agent must be\nable to SEE a problem it cannot yet act on — reporting it and saying so is the\ncontract, silently ignoring it is not.","files":null}]}